  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nAdditional rounds of showers and thunderstorms are expected to \nmove through the area today through Monday night, with most \nrobust activity occurring in concert with a couple of \nshortwaves.\n\nActivity will be isolated to scattered this afternoon, then the next \nround of more widespread activity arrives this evening. A Flood \nWatch has been issued for southeast Ohio and much of West Virginia, \nwhere heavy downpours could rapidly produce a couple inches of rain \novernight and Monday morning. Locations that already received heavy \nrain earlier today will be at greatest risk for flash flooding \novernight. Additional rain on Monday could necessitate an \nextension to the Flood Watch. A few strong to severe storms \ncould also be capable of producing locally strong wind gusts.\n\nFrom Tuesday through Thursday, the pattern remains unsettled with \nadditional chances for flooding as an upper trough spirals across \nthe Middle Ohio Valley towards the east coast. Drier conditions \nreturn late week into the weekend as the system pushes off the \nAtlantic Coast.",
